.SH NAME
mmchek \- check usage of mm macros and eqn delimiters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mmchek
[\^files\^]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Mmchek\^
is a program for checking
the contents of the named 
.I files\^
for errors in
the use of Memorandum Macros
(see
.IR mm (1))
and
some
.IR eqn (1)
constructions.
Appropriate messages are produced.
The program skips all directories, and, 
if no file name is given, standard input is read.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
eqn(1),
mm(1),
mmt(1).
.br
.I "MM\-Memorandum Macros\^"
by D. W. Smith and J. R. Mashey.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Unreadable files result in the message ``Cannot open 
.IR "file-name" '' 
being returned.
The remaining output of the program is a  
diagnostic of the source file.
.SH LIMITATIONS 
This is an experimental version of
.IR mmchek .
.I Mmchek\^
may be fully supported in the future.
